{"id":"016ffefd9b733e65","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-thm-borel-measurability.md","title":"Borel Measurability","display":"thm-borel-measurability — Borel Measurability","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-borel-measurability","aliases":["58-thm-borel-measurability"],"display":"thm-borel-measurability — Borel Measurability","depends_on":["[[58-df-borel]]","[[58-df-lebesgue]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-borel-measurability"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-borel-measurability</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-borel-measurability — Borel Measurability"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"9375de7089953a2b\" href=\"?note=9375de7089953a2b\" title=\"58-df-borel\">58-df-borel</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"58-df-lebesgue\">58-df-lebesgue</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Borel}\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\operatorname{Borel}\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\">\\(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}\">\\(A \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}\\)</span> (子集)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}}\\)</span> is the Euclidean topology on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Borel}(-,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})\">\\(\\mathrm{Borel}(-,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})\\)</span> is the Borel-set predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"9375de7089953a2b\" href=\"?note=9375de7089953a2b\" title=\"58-df-borel\">58-df-borel</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda^*\">\\(\\lambda^*\\)</span> are the Lebesgue-measurability predicate and Lebesgue outer measure from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"58-df-lebesgue\">58-df-lebesgue</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borel\\text{-}measurability} \\vdash \\mathrm{Borel}(A,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})\\to\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borel\\text{-}measurability} \\vdash \\mathrm{Borel}(A,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})\\to\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borel\\text{-}measurability} \\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\\to\\exists B\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Borel}(B,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})\\land\\lambda^*(A\\mathbin\\triangle B)=0\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borel\\text{-}measurability} \\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\\to\\exists B\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Borel}(B,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})\\land\\lambda^*(A\\mathbin\\triangle B)=0\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every Borel set is Lebesgue measurable.</li>\n<li>Conversely, every Lebesgue-measurable set differs from a Borel set by a set of outer measure zero; this expresses completion of the Borel measure.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-borel","status":"resolved","id":"9375de7089953a2b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-borel]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-lebesgue","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-lebesgue]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-borel","status":"resolved","id":"9375de7089953a2b","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Borel}(-,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})$ is the Borel-set predicate from [[58-df-borel]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-lebesgue","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S$ and $\\lambda^*$ are the Lebesgue-measurability predicate and Lebesgue outer measure from [[58-df-lebesgue]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\operatorname{Borel}\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S\\subseteq V^{1}","display":false},{"tex":"A \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Borel}(-,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda^*","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borel\\text{-}measurability} \\vdash \\mathrm{Borel}(A,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})\\to\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borel\\text{-}measurability} \\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\\to\\exists B\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Borel}(B,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathrm{eucl}})\\land\\lambda^*(A\\mathbin\\triangle B)=0\\bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1382,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4053","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-thm-borel-measurability.md|58-thm-borel-measurability]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["9375de7089953a2b","68427bc628af9b8d"]}